From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] NetworkCommon: hold off binding until the platform opens the
 gate

A USB NIC that binds during EfiBootManagerConnectAll drags the whole
network stack into existence in the middle of boot option enumeration.
On this platform the NIC is the BMC's CDC gadget - the Redfish host
interface - so what actually springs to life is RedfishDiscoverDxe,
RedfishConfigHandlerDriver and RpiRedfishSyncDxe's HTTP exchange, all of
it running from timer and protocol-notify callbacks at TPL_CALLBACK and
TPL_NOTIFY. TPL is strictly priority-scheduled: BDS at TPL_APPLICATION
resumes only when all of that drains. Behind the DWC2 USB-C controller,
where every USB transfer is a TPL_NOTIFY busy-wait, enumeration slowed
to a visible crawl (patches 0030-0032 in the edk2-platforms recipe made
the individual transfers honest, but the co-scheduling is structural).

The connect-all does not need this NIC: it must never be a boot target
(patch 0103 already keeps it out of the boot options), and nothing in
boot option enumeration reads from it. So let the platform choose the
moment. NetworkCommonSupported returns EFI_UNSUPPORTED until the
platform installs the gate protocol - a bare GUID, no interface - after
which binding proceeds exactly as before. NetworkCommon is the single
choke point for all three CDC class drivers (ECM, NCM, RNDIS produce
the USB Ethernet protocol; only NetworkCommon consumes it), and it is
where the notification endpoint is armed and the UNDI/SNP chain starts,
so gating here keeps the wire completely quiet.

The platform half lives in PlatformBootManagerLib (edk2-platforms patch
0034): it installs the gate and connects the USB Ethernet handles after
boot option enumeration, so the Redfish stack comes up during the boot
timeout countdown instead of on top of the enumeration. The GUID literal
is duplicated there; keep the two in sync.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform boot-policy gate]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbNetwork/NetworkCommon/DriverBinding.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Bus/Usb/UsbNetwork/NetworkCommon/DriverBinding.c
@@ -14,6 +14,24 @@
 UINT32       gRateLimitingPollTimer;
 BOOLEAN      gRateLimitingEnable;
 
+//
+// Platform gate: NetworkCommonSupported refuses to bind until some platform
+// agent installs this protocol (a bare GUID, no interface).
+//
+// A USB NIC that binds during the boot manager's connect-all drags the whole
+// network stack -- and, on Redfish host interface platforms, the Redfish
+// discovery and configuration machinery -- into existence in the middle of
+// boot option enumeration, where its timer- and protocol-notify-driven work
+// preempts BDS at TPL_APPLICATION for as long as it runs. The platform
+// decides when that cost is welcome by installing the gate and connecting
+// the USB Ethernet handles itself.
+//
+// The GUID literal is duplicated in the platform's PlatformBootManagerLib
+// (edk2-platforms is a separate tree); keep the two in sync.
+//
+STATIC CONST EFI_GUID  mUsbNicGateGuid =
+  { 0x5144a8c6, 0x4d1c, 0x4709, { 0xb3, 0xa6, 0xfc, 0xb7, 0x44, 0xc3, 0x60, 0xdc } };
+
 EFI_DRIVER_BINDING_PROTOCOL  gNetworkCommonDriverBinding = {
   NetworkCommonSupported,
   NetworkCommonDriverStart,
@@ -103,6 +121,11 @@
 {
   EFI_STATUS                   Status;
   EDKII_USB_ETHERNET_PROTOCOL  *UsbEth;
+  VOID                         *UsbNicGate;
+
+  if (EFI_ERROR (gBS->LocateProtocol ((EFI_GUID *)&mUsbNicGateGuid, NULL, &UsbNicGate))) {
+    return EFI_UNSUPPORTED;
+  }
 
   Status = gBS->OpenProtocol (
                   ControllerHandle,
